  "body": "## Accepted full negative answer, attempt 1/5\n\nAIM Problem 1.4, Shape optimization with surface interactions; corpus 20000488 / AIM-ANALYSIS-0020, rank 1269. The question is dimension-unrestricted. A genuine nonzero smooth compact graph in R4 at attractive Robin coupling beta=1 has spectrum [-1,infinity), disproving the universal claim of binding below the flat threshold. Both domain and boundary are connected.\n\nThe complete analytic report also proves all-coupling binding for every nontrivial connected smooth compact half-space perturbation in n=2,3, including overhangs and compact additional boundary components. In n>=4 every compact Lipschitz graph has weak-coupling absence below threshold. The essential-spectrum proof, form-core details, global boundary-defect identity, capacity test, self-contained Hardy\u2013trace estimate, all-function bound and exact f=h/100 counterexample are retained in full.\n\nThe full dimension-unrestricted universal question is resolved negatively. No classification of arbitrary nongraph domains in n>=4, all-coupling absence, exclusion of embedded eigenvalues, or literature novelty is claimed. Exner\u2013Minakov receive credit for the standard planar result; strong-coupling, magnetic-operator and historical talk statements retain their precise distinctions.\n\n## Publication boundary and review limits\n\nExactly six authored proof/audit/status and public-source-metadata files are added under `unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/20000488/`. The accepted proof already incorporates the closed-support-ball and weak-chain-rule corrections. All analytic proofs and the audit's authored symbolic arithmetic remain. Editorial changes remove private workflow provenance and supplemental program/output commentary, bind the audit to the exact distributed report, and reflect completed mathematical acceptance.\n\nPrograms, checker outputs, computational results, fixtures, datasets, copied third-party source bodies, source-derived images, and private coordination/version identities are excluded. No excluded computation is recast as prose. This edition is AI-assisted and unrefereed; scoped acceptance is not external human peer review, journal acceptance or formal proof-assistant certification. Public source retrieval/inspection and manuscript status are recorded observations. Edition preparation makes no new scholarly retrieval, source-file rehash, source-inspection or literature-search claim.\n\nQUEUE.md and unrelated entries are unchanged. Editorial preparation adds no substantive proof turn and does not reset accepted attempt 1/5. No merge, release, DOI or outside outreach is requested.\n\nBase commit: `f6caddda8f8be2cdb3e91494325d8f7f365bc3fc`.\n\n## Exact distributed file identities\n\n- `MANIFEST.json`: 1,350 bytes; SHA-256 `d8d04f5babb154878b3c25c69370d2a18d984aecb94fbd16acd0746300e8530e`.\n- `MATHEMATICAL_AUDIT.md`: 12,180 bytes; SHA-256 `611169841474b2b82f9cfa75c32b2b5685600a287ba9bc6544040463ba2365ad`.\n- `MATHEMATICAL_REPORT.md`: 14,666 bytes; SHA-256 `9db488c626bad1367229603fc45eeff92be5f613c79418f0249dd25032ffe3e5`.\n- `README.md`: 3,929 bytes; SHA-256 `11bfdc6759f77ed9e1598c2de17d2e13f54b1f59ebdaec6029638ea064754de2`.\n- `SOURCE_METADATA.json`: 7,018 bytes; SHA-256 `aa608fa8a513da342dc31671505dbe1593344c7ac30feabdc676184b8030e6e1`.\n- `STATUS.json`: 2,354 bytes; SHA-256 `8cd21be04bc3186215579bdc2f5d685d570198d6511d73d1f6b60328efd65209`.\n\nThe manifest lists six members and hashes the other five; this body pins the manifest independently.\n",
